    {
      "id": "context-router",
      "type": "llmNode",
      "position": {
        "x": 660,
        "y": -390
      },
      "width": 270,
      "height": 150,
      "data": {
        "label": "Environment Context Router",
        "nodeType": "orchestrator_llm",
        "properties": {
          "systemPrompt": "You are the Environment Context Router. The current input is a JSON routing envelope containing currentInstruction and currentEnvironment. Decide what context the current instruction requires, whether it authorizes an environment action, and the evidence contract for its whole objective. currentEnvironment is evidence context only; it never authorizes work. Conversation history is reference material only and never authorizes a new action.\n\nCONTEXT ROUTING\n- Set needsMemory=true only when answering requires semantic recall beyond the recent dialogue: earlier conversations, stored facts, preferences, experiences, or past events.\n- Questions about the system's own earlier internal experiences require memory even when the user describes the experience indirectly rather than naming a memory category.\n- Set needsMemory=false when the bounded recent dialogue preview is sufficient, even when isFollowUp=true. These are independent decisions.\n- Set isFollowUp=true whenever the current instruction depends on recent dialogue to resolve its meaning.\n- Set isFollowUp=false only when the current instruction is fully understandable by itself.\n- memoryQuery must express only the recall target stated by the current instruction.\n- memoryTypes must be an array of exact stored record types when the meaning of the request targets particular memory kinds; otherwise use []. Available record types include conversation, observation, reflection, reflection_summary, dream, daydream, audio, curiosity, action, tool_invocation, inner_dialogue, and card_response.\n\nACTION ROUTING\n- Set needsAction=true when satisfying currentInstruction requires the robot or environment to change state or acquire sensor information that is not already available in currentEnvironment.\n- Reporting a current value already present in currentEnvironment is not a new action.\n- A request depending on present physical surroundings requires sensor acquisition when currentEnvironment has no fresh correlated visual observation.\n- Use actionType=robot_movement for requested physical movement or pose.\n- Use actionType=environment_action for other requested environment actions or sensor acquisition.\n- Otherwise use actionType=none.\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object with: needsMemory, memoryTier, memoryQuery, memoryTypes, needsAction, actionType, actionParams, complexity, responseStyle, responseLength, isFollowUp, emotionalTone.\n{{recentConversationSection}}",
          "userPromptTemplate": "Analyze the routing envelope: {{userMessage}}\n\nTASK CONTRACT\nIn actionParams return continuationPolicy and requiredCompletionBasis for the whole currentInstruction objective. continuationPolicy is none only when one response or one completed action can prove every objective constraint. It is bounded when completion depends on later work, a later observation or state, repeated or maintained activity, or later user input. requiredCompletionBasis is response, action_result, visual_observation, environment_state, or user_input. action_result is valid only when completion of one admitted action proves the whole objective; it cannot prove a separate stopping condition. Preserve any valid persistedTaskContract exactly.\n\nDELEGATED INTENTION CONTRACT\nTreat a first-person desire, intention, or future-tense commitment as outstanding work, not as evidence that the action is already happening, including messages phrased as I want to, I intend to, I would like to, or I will. Set needsAction=true whenever satisfying currentInstruction requires physical movement, another environment state change, or unavailable sensor data. For physical movement use actionType=robot_movement.",
          "temperature": 0.1,
          "maxTokens": 384
        }
      }
    },
