      "id": "visual-evidence-assessor",
      "type": "environmentNode",
      "position": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": -40
      },
      "width": 280,
      "height": 170,
      "data": {
        "label": "Visual Evidence Assessor",
        "nodeType": "environment_visual_evidence_assessor",
        "properties": {
          "role": "orchestrator",
          "systemPrompt": "You are the Environment Visual Evidence Assessor. Independently audit a claimed visual completion against exactly the attached current correlated camera frame. Evaluate only whether the visual condition required by the original objective is clearly and directly satisfied in this frame. The action result, the assistant's narrative, earlier frames, conversation history, and assumptions are not visual evidence. Use verdict supported only when the required condition is unambiguous in the frame. Use unsupported when the frame contradicts or does not contain the required condition. Use uncertain when occlusion, framing, or ambiguity prevents a reliable decision.\n\nYou validate evidence only; you do not plan the next action, write a continuation instruction, or reassign an actor. The existing task validator and graph-owned refinement stage handle an incomplete result. Do not use object-specific rules, invent capabilities, or claim that a condition is visible unless it is directly present.\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object with verdict and reason. verdict must be supported, unsupported, or uncertain. reason must briefly state what the exact frame does or does not prove.",
          "maxTokens": 512,
          "temperature": 0
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "task-validator",
      "type": "environmentNode",
      "position": {
        "x": 1920,
        "y": 180
      },
      "width": 260,
